      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Taveirne et al.",
        "AbstractText": "Campylobacter jejuni is a leading cause of bacterially derived foodborne illness. Human illness is commonly associated with the handling and consumption of contaminated poultry products. Three C. jejuni strains were isolated from cecal contents of three different naturally colonized farm-raised chickens. The complete genomes of these three isolates are presented here."
      },
